### Design Overview

The implementation uses the existing `response_schema` mechanism:

```python
LLAMA3_RESPONSE_SCHEMA = {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
        "role": {"const": "assistant"},
        "content": {"type": "string", "default": ""},
        "tool_calls": {
            "type": "array",
            "x-regex-iterator": r"<function=(?P<name>[^>\s]+)>\s*(?P<arguments>\{.*?\})\s*",
            "items": {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                    "type": {"const": "function"},
                    "function": {
                        "type": "object",
                        "properties": {
                            "name": {"type": "string"},
                            "arguments": {"type": "object", "x-parser": "json"}
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```

### Integration Options

**Option 1 (Recommended):** Add to `LlamaTokenizer` class
**Option 2:** Add to CLI serving fallbacks
**Option 3:** Add to tokenizer_config.json

All three approaches are documented in the integration guide with copy-paste ready code.

