## ORM Integration Types (Prisma/TypeORM)

```typescript
// For Prisma users
export namespace Prisma {
  export type UserGetPayload<T> = T extends { include: { participants: true } }
    ? User & { participants: Participant[] }
    : User;

  export type MessageGetPayload<T> = T extends { 
    include: { 
      sender: true; 
      attachments: true;
      reactions: true;
    } 
  }
    ? Message & { 
        sender: User | null;
        attachments: Attachment[];
        reactions: MessageReaction[];
      }
    : Message;
}

// For TypeORM users
export interface UserEntity extends User {
  participants?: Participant[];
  sentMessages?: Message[];
  blockedUsers?: BlockedUser[];
  blockedBy?: BlockedUser[];
}

export interface ConversationEntity extends Conversation {
  participants?: Participant[];
  messages?: Message[];
  creator?: User;
}
```

These types provide:
1. **Full type safety** for all database operations
2. **Clear contracts** for API responses
3. **Support for both** runtime and compile-time checks
4. **Easy integration** with ORMs and query builders
5. **Real-time event typing** for WebSocket communications

